---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import site from '../../site.config.json' with { type: 'json' };
const page = {
  url: '/terms/', title: 'Terms and Conditions', seoTitle: 'Terms and Conditions',
  pageType: 'legal', status: 'ready', author: site.defaultAuthor, reviewer: null,
  needsReviewer: false, parent: '/', parentTitle: 'Home',
  schema: ['WebPage'], updated: site.legalUpdated, indexable: true,
  blockers: [], headings: [], faqs: [],
  description: 'Terms for using MarineDieselEngine.com.au. Information is general in nature and is not a substitute for a licensed marine mechanic.',
};
---
<Page page={page}>
  <h1>Terms and conditions</h1>
  <p>
    These terms apply to your use of {site.name}. If you do not accept them,
    please do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} publishes general information about marine diesel engines in
    Australia, and lists marine businesses. <strong>We do not work on boats, sell
    parts, or perform any of the work described here.</strong> We are not a
    party to any arrangement you make with a business you find through this
    site.
  </p>

  <h2>Information is general, not advice for your engine</h2>
  <p>
    Everything here is general information. It is written carefully, but it
    cannot account for your specific vessel, engine, installation or
    circumstances, and it is not a substitute for a licensed marine mechanic
    inspecting your engine.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Marine engine faults can be dangerous.</strong> Some can cause fire,
    flooding, or leave you without propulsion at sea. Where a page tells you to
    stop the engine and get professional help, that is the advice — do not
    substitute your own judgement based on a general guide.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are responsible for deciding what to do with your vessel. Do not rely on
    this site alone for a decision that affects safety.
  </p>

  <h2>Prices</h2>
  <p>
    Price ranges are collected from Australian businesses and are dated on the
    page. They are indicative only. Real quotes vary with access, vessel, engine,
    location and what is found once work starts. A price on this site is not an
    offer, a quote, or a promise that anyone will do the work for that amount.
  </p>

  <h2>Business listings</h2>
  <p>
    We verify listings before publishing them and re-check them periodically,
    but we do not guarantee that any listed business is available, appropriately
    licensed or insured for your work, or suitable for it. Satisfy yourself
    before engaging anyone. Check licences and insurance directly with the
    business and the relevant authority.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where a listing involves a paid referral relationship, we say so on the
    listing itself. Payment never buys a higher position within a page.
  </p>
  <p>
    A listing is not an endorsement, and the absence of a business is not a
    judgement about it.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    We link to other sites for your convenience. We do not control them and are
    not responsible for their content, their practices, or anything you do
    there.
  </p>

  <h2>Your consumer rights</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or modifies any consumer guarantee
    or right you have under the Australian Consumer Law or any other law that
    cannot be excluded. Where a right cannot be excluded, these terms apply only
    to the extent they are consistent with it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Subject to that, and to the extent the law allows, we are not liable for loss
    or damage arising from your use of this site or from your reliance on
    information published here.
  </p>

  <h2>Our content</h2>
  <p>
    The writing, structure and data on this site belong to us. You are welcome to
    read it, print it for your own use, and link to it. Republishing it — in
    whole or in substantial part, including reproducing it as your own content —
    requires our permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If something here is wrong, tell us. We would rather fix it than leave it.
    Send corrections to <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and governing law</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms; the current version is always the one on this
    page, dated below. These terms are governed by the laws of Australia.
  </p>
</Page>
